2Ki 6:1 , Elisha, giving leave to the young prophets to enlarge their dwellings, causes iron to swim;
2Ki 6:8 , He discloses the king of Syria's counsel;
2Ki 6:13 , The army which was sent to Dothan to apprehend Elisha, is smitten with blindness;
2Ki 6:19 , Being brought into Samaria, they are dismissed in peace;
2Ki 6:24 , The famine in Samaria causes women to eat their own children;
2Ki 6:30 , The king sends to slay Elisha.
